# Resources

Resources live under `common-resources/src/commonMain/composeResources/`. Generated accessor: `dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.resources.Res`.

## Strings

`composeResources/values/strings.xml`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<resources>
    <string name="guides_top_bar_title">Guides</string>
    <string name="guides_filter_hero">Hero</string>
</resources>
```

Usage:

```kotlin
import dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.resources.Res
import dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.resources.guides_top_bar_title
import org.jetbrains.compose.resources.stringResource

Text(text = stringResource(Res.string.guides_top_bar_title))
```

Naming: `{feature}_{element}_{description}`. Shared strings: `{element}_{description}`.

No hardcoded user-facing strings in composables. Logs and debug text are allowed inline.

## Fonts

`composeResources/font/` holds custom typeface files. Loaded via `Font(Res.font.{name})` in `theme/Type.kt`.

## JSON Constants

`composeResources/files/constants/{heroes,items,abilities}.json` ship statically with the app. Read at runtime via `Res.readBytes("files/constants/heroes.json")`, then decode with `kotlinx.serialization.json.Json` configured in `ConstantResourcesDataSource`.

If a JSON file grows past a few hundred KB or starts to need frequent updates, move it to Supabase Storage (similar to icons) — bundling large blobs slows down the build and bloats every release.

## Migration note

The project does **not** use moko-resources today; do not import `dev.icerock.moko.resources.*` types. A migration to moko-resources is planned (see `mobile-roadmap.mdc`). Until then, all resource access goes through Compose's `Res.*` API.
